<div class="page">
  <div class="section-title">VOLUNTARY ACCIDENTAL DEATH &amp; DISMEMBERMENT (AD&amp;D) INSURANCE</div>
  <p style="font-size: 10pt;">This benefit provides you the opportunity to purchase Voluntary Accidental Death and Dismemberment (AD&amp;D) Insurance for yourself and your family. This program provides benefits when death is caused by an accident and provides an accidental dismemberment and paralysis benefit. If you wish to elect voluntary AD&amp;D, you may not elect it without life insurance coverage. For example, if you wish to elect $100,000 in voluntary AD&amp;D coverage, you must also elect $100,000 in voluntary life coverage. Please note: You may not elect this benefit for your spouse and dependents if you do not elect it for yourself as an employee.</p>

  <div class="section-title">Available Benefits</div>
  <ul class="bullet-list">
    <li>Employee Coverage – An amount between $10,000 and $500,000, in increments of $10,000. Maximum employee coverage is 5 times your Basic Annual Earnings.</li>
    <li>Spouse Coverage – An amount between $10,000 and $100,000, in increments of $10,000. Maximum spouse coverage is 100% of the employee's amount of Basic and Optional Life insurance combined. Coverage ends when your spouse turns 70.</li>
    <li>Dependent Child(ren) Coverage – An amount between $2,500 and $10,000, in increments of $2,500 for each eligible dependent child to age 26.</li>
  </ul>

  <div class="section-title">Costs</div>
