    </tbody>
  </table>

  <p style="font-size: 10pt;">To calculate your cost of Employee or Spouse coverage, follow this simple formula:</p>

  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>$</th>
        <th>+</th>
        <th>$1,000</th>
        <th>x</th>
        <th>$</th>
        <th>RATE PER PAY FOR EMPLOYEE OR SPOUSE AGE</th>
        <th>=</th>
        <th>$</th>
        <th>COST PER PAY (24 DEDUCTIONS)</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td>$</td>
        <td>+</td>
        <td>$1,000</td>
        <td>x</td>
        <td>$</td>
        <td></td>
        <td>=</td>
        <td>$</td>
        <td></td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <p style="font-size: 10pt;">$ <span data-field="monthly_cost_formula_variable_1">{{ monthly_cost_formula_variable_1 }}</span> + $1,000 x $ <span data-field="monthly_cost_formula_variable_2">{{ monthly_cost_formula_variable_2 }}</span> = $ <span data-field="monthly_cost_formula_result">{{ monthly_cost_formula_result }}</span></p>
</div>

<div class="page">
  <div class="section-title">FLEXIBLE SPENDING ACCOUNTS</div>

  <div class="section-title">Medical Spending Account (FSA) – 1/1/21 to 12/31/21 Plan Year</div>
  <p style="font-size: 10pt;">The Medical Spending Account is a pre-tax savings account to be used for qualified medical, dental and vision expenses for you and your eligible dependents. Per the IRS, an employee may elect up to $2,750 for the 2021 calendar year. <span data-field="fsa_eligibility_note">{{ fsa_eligibility_note }}</span></p>
  <p style="font-size: 10pt;">FSA contains a Use It or Lose It provision – plan carefully!</p>

  <div class="section-title">Dependent Care Spending Account (DCA) – 1/1/21 to 12/31/21 Plan Year</div>
  <p style="font-size: 10pt;">The Dependent Care Spending Account is a pre-tax savings account for elder care and child care expenses. You must be using daycare services so that you and your spouse can work. In addition, your provider of care must furnish you with his/her Social Security Number or Tax Identification Number. By law, the maximum amount that you may contribute to any Dependent Care Spending Account for your family is $5,000 each Plan Year. Per the IRS, an employee may elect up to $5,000 for the 2021 calendar year. <span data-field="dca_eligibility_note">{{ dca_eligibility_note }}</span></p>
  <p style="font-size: 10pt;">DCA contains a Use It or Lose It provision – plan carefully!</p>

  <div class="section-title">Limited Purpose Spending Account (LPSA) – 1/1/21 to 12/31/21 Plan Year</div>
  <p style="font-size: 10pt;">The Limited Purpose Spending Account is a pre-tax savings account to be used for qualified dental and vision expenses only for you and your eligible dependents. Per the IRS, an employee may elect up to $2,750 for the 2021 calendar year. <span data-field="lpsa_eligibility_note">{{ lpsa_eligibility_note }}</span></p>
  <p style="font-size: 10pt;">LPSA contains a Use It or Lose It provision – plan carefully!</p>

  <div class="section-title">Health Savings Account (HSA) – 1/1/21 to 12/31/21 Plan Year</div>
  <p style="font-size: 10pt;">The Health Savings Account is a pre-tax savings account to be used for qualified medical, dental and vision expenses for you and your eligible dependents. Per the IRS, an employee may elect up to $3,600 single or $7,200 family for the 2021 calendar year. These limits include funds from Wilkes University and any employee contributions. Employees $5+ can contribute an additional $1,000 catch up limit ear calendar year. Your HSA contributions are not taxable income. The HSA is a tax-advantaged account (not FDIC insured) and your secondary plan is NOT another HDHP. You are ineligible to enroll in the Health Savings Account and receive funding (employer and employee). <span data-field="hsa_eligibility_note">{{ hsa_eligibility_note }}</span></p>
  <p style="font-size: 10pt;">An HSA is not a Use-It-or-Lose-It account.</p>
</div>




<div class="page">
  <div class="section-title">SMARTSHOPPER</div>
  <p>Vitals SmartShopper is a new program offered by {{ program_provider }} that lets you shop for lower-cost health care and choose from several possibilities. Vitals SmartShopper is for all employees and their dependents enrolled in the {{ plan_name }} Plan and the {{ plan_name_2 }} Plan.</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Compare costs and quality for common medical procedures</li>
    <li>Use the information provided to help estimate out of pocket costs</li>
    <li>Earn cash rewards while shopping for care</li>
    <li>Save money and make the most efficient use of your health care benefits</li>
  </ul>

  <div class="section-title">TUITION REMISSION</div>
  <p>{{ university_name }} Undergraduate and graduate credits to all full-time employees, spouses, same-gender domestic partners, and dependent sons and daughters after the employee has completed (90) ninety calendar days of service. The tuition benefit covers 100% of the actual tuition cost. The employee is responsible for applicable fees and textbook costs.</p>

  <p>Other Tuition Programs: {{ other_tuition_program_name }}.</p>
  <p>Please refer to the Staff Policies Manual for a complete description of the tuition benefits and eligibility requirements.</p>

  <div class="section-title">RETIREMENT SAVINGS PLAN</div>
  <ul>
    <li>Provider: {{ retirement_provider }}</li>
    <li>Plan Type: {{ retirement_plan_type }}</li>
    <li>Contributions: Effective {{ contribution_start_date }}, the {{ company_name }} contributes {{ contribution_percentage }}% of your base pay, provided you contribute a minimum of {{ minimum_contribution_percentage }}% (subject to change). Effective {{ contribution_effective_date }}, the University has suspended its contribution into your retirement account (subject to change). For more information, please contact {{ contact_person }} at {{ contact_phone }}.</li>
    <li>Eligibility: Employees hired on or after September 1, 2012, one (1) year of Eligibility of Service shall be required (subject to change). Employees hired before September 1, 2012 the first of the month coinciding with or next following 90 days of hire (subject to change).</li>
    <li>University Matching Contributions Vesting: Employees hired on or after September 1, 2012, shall be vested according to the following schedule: 0% vesting for less than one (1) year of service, 20% vesting for at least one (1) year of service, 40% vesting for at least two (2) years of service, 60% vesting for at least three (3) years of service, 80% vesting for at least four (4) years of service, and 100% vesting for five (5) or more years of service (subject to change). Employees hired prior to 9/1/12 shall be 100% and immediately vested.</li>
  </ul>
</div>

